s and treatment of rumination syndrome.", "ELECTROMYOGRAPHY:Electromyography is a diagnostic tool that can be useful in assessing abdominal wall function in patients with rumination syndrome.", "MANOMETRY:Manometry is a diagnostic test that measures the pressure within the esophagus and can help in diagnosing rumination syndrome.", "IMPEDANCE:Impedance is a diagnostic technique that can be combined with high resolution manometry to evaluate esophageal conditions.", "ELECTROMYOGRAPHY OF ABDOMINAL WALL:Electromyography of the abdominal wall is a diagnostic tool that helps assess muscle function in patients with gastrointestinal disorders.", "NUTRITIONAL FORMULAS:Nutritional formulas are specialized dietary products specifically designed to meet the nutritional needs of patients, particularly those with specific health conditions such as diabetes and dietary restrictions. These products provide essential nutrients and are often utilized in clinical settings for patients who may be unable to consume food orally. They are particularly beneficial for individuals with medical needs, including those with diabetes mellitus and rumination syndrome, as they help improve metabolic control. Overall, nutritional formulas serve as a vital resource for ensuring adequate nutrition in patients with various health challenges.", "HIGH RESOLUTION MANOMETRY:", "ADENOCARCINOMA PANCREATICO DUCTAL:Adenocarcinoma pancreático ductal is the most common form of pancreatic cancer, known for its aggressive nature and low survival rates.", "BICI:BICI is a comprehensive treatment protocol and medical device designed for managing insulin delivery in patients with diabetes, particularly in oncology settings. It stands for \"Infusor subcutáneo continuo de insulina,\" which translates to a continuous subcutaneous insulin infuser. This device is specifically utilized to assist in the management of severe hypoglycemia in diabetic patients, ensuring a consistent and effective delivery of insulin to maintain optimal blood glucose levels.", "SÍNDROME PARANEOPLÁSICO:Síndrome paraneoplásico refers to a set of symptoms that occur in patients with cancer, which are not directly related to the local presence of the tumor.", "CA 19.9:CA 19.9 is a tumor marker that plays a crucial role in the diagnosis and monitoring of treatment for pancreatic cancer. It has a sensitivity and specificity of up to 92%, making it a valuable tool in the clinical assessment of this type of cancer.", "NM ABDOMINAL:NM abdominal is a medical procedure reserved for difficult cases, cystic neoplasms, and evaluation of bile ducts.", "PANCREATECTOMY DUODENAL:Pancreatectomy duodenal is a surgical procedure of choice for tumors located in the head of the pancreas."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}